<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n88259" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πρόπᾱς</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πᾱσα</span>,
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πᾰν</span>, in <i><span class="en">
			Hom.
		</span></i> and <i><span class="en">
			Hes.
		</span></i> mostly <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">π. ἦμαρ</span>
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>all</i> day <i>long,</i>
			where <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πρό</span> 'on and on' goes with the
			verb, <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				1.601
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				9.161
			</span></i>, al.; hence <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πρόπας</span> becomes
			merely a strengthd. form of <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πᾶς,</span>
			once in <i><span class="en">
				Hom.
			</span></i>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νῆας προπάσας</span>
			<i>all</i> the ships <i>together,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Il.
				2.493
			</span></i>; freq. in Trag., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πρόπασα χώρα,
				γαῖα,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Pr.</u>
				407
			</span></i> (lyr.), <i><span class="en">
				<u>Pers.</u>
				548
			</span></i> (lyr.); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">π. δόμος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Ag.</u>
					1011
				</span></i>
			 (lyr.); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πρόπαντος χρόνου</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Eu.</u>
					898
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">π. στόλος, πότμος,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>OT</u>
				169
			</span></i> (lyr.), <i><span class="en">
				<u>Ant.</u>
				859
			</span></i> (lyr.); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πρόπαντα κακὰ κακῶν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>OC</u>
					1237
				</span></i>
			 (lyr.); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">π. γέννα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>Or.</u>
					972
				</span></i>
			 (lyr.); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">π. ἑσμός</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>Pae.Delph.</u>
					14
				</span></i>
			: neut. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πρόπαν</span> as
			Adv., <i>utterly,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Ph.</u>
				1504
			</span></i> (lyr.).</div>
